{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LNLu8LkA7YiEBiHgQ2xpb7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:docs.mistral.ai vibe code web limits lifecycle\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Limits and lifecycle | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/limits-and-lifecycle\"},{\"title\":\"Projects | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/projects\"},{\"title\":\"Sessions | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/sessions\"},{\"title\":\"Sandbox environment | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/sandbox-environment\"},{\"title\":\"Choose CLI, VS Code, or web sessions | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/choose-cli-vscode-web-sessions\"},{\"title\":\"Work with the CLI | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/work-with-cli\"},{\"title\":\"Vibe Code | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Install and setup | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/install-setup\"},{\"title\":\"Security | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/security\"},{\"title\":\"Get started | Mistral Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/le-chat/content-creation/vibe-code-workflow\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Vibe Code Web limits and lifecycle:\n\n## Session Definition and Lifecycle\n\nA Vibe Code Web session is one run of the Vibe Code agent against a GitHub repository in a managed cloud sandbox. This covers how a session starts, what state it can be in, what persists, what gets deleted, and which limits apply.\n\n## Session Continuation\n\nA pushed branch or pull request doesn't end the session automatically. You can keep iterating by sending follow-up prompts, reviewer comments, or CI failures.\n\n## Session Persistence After Completion\n\nGitHub branches and pull requests already created by Vibe Code Web remain in your repository. However, session history can be inspected after a run, but inactive sessions cannot be resumed once the sandbox has been deprovisioned.\n\n## Session Limits\n\nSession limits can depend on your plan and rollout status.\n\n## Sandbox Behavior\n\nEach Vibe Code Web session runs in an isolated cloud sandbox provisioned for that run and deleted when the session ends.\n\nFor more detailed information, you can visit the [full documentation page](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/limits-and-lifecycle).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"539cacdc-2e48-4ba3-b4b0-e5e4a8a2ae1c","uuid":"1ad47046-7473-4a82-a38c-27149007ad46","timestamp":"2026-09-11T19:43:59.508Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:docs.mistral.ai vibe code web limits lifecycle","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01213Vdg3ef7c4p1TuGwdcFH","content":[{"title":"Limits and lifecycle | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/limits-and-lifecycle"},{"title":"Projects | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/projects"},{"title":"Sessions | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/sessions"},{"title":"Sandbox environment | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/sandbox-environment"},{"title":"Choose CLI, VS Code, or web sessions | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/choose-cli-vscode-web-sessions"},{"title":"Work with the CLI | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/work-with-cli"},{"title":"Vibe Code | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/overview"},{"title":"Install and setup | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/install-setup"},{"title":"Security | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/security"},{"title":"Get started | Mistral Docs","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/le-chat/content-creation/vibe-code-workflow"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about Vibe Code Web limits and lifecycle:\n\n## Session Definition and Lifecycle\n\nA Vibe Code Web session is one run of the Vibe Code agent against a GitHub repository in a managed cloud sandbox. This covers how a session starts, what state it can be in, what persists, what gets deleted, and which limits apply.\n\n## Session Continuation\n\nA pushed branch or pull request doesn't end the session automatically. You can keep iterating by sending follow-up prompts, reviewer comments, or CI failures.\n\n## Session Persistence After Completion\n\nGitHub branches and pull requests already created by Vibe Code Web remain in your repository. However, session history can be inspected after a run, but inactive sessions cannot be resumed once the sandbox has been deprovisioned.\n\n## Session Limits\n\nSession limits can depend on your plan and rollout status.\n\n## Sandbox Behavior\n\nEach Vibe Code Web session runs in an isolated cloud sandbox provisioned for that run and deleted when the session ends.\n\nFor more detailed information, you can visit the [full documentation page](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/vibe-code-web/limits-and-lifecycle)."],"durationSeconds":6.372982097999999,"searchCount":1}}
